IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`
IMPORT `coa12-ch7-definitions`

-- coa12-ch3a-report.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 16, Chapter 3, "Auditor's report" and the first of "Duties and rights
-- of auditors": ss 495, 496, 497, 497A, 498, 498A (lines 6970-7049 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nobody's point of view; the seat layer is coa12-seat.l4.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- Quote lines are copied by work/gen.py from that file and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the rulings of 2026-11-04/05, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words. Each such branch carries -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     not covered. Each such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
-- Two kinds of function in this module. A DUTY function ("must ...") answers whether the party is obliged on the facts: JUST FALSE
-- where the section's own "where"/"if" trigger is unmet (fork F1). A CONTENT function ("the report includes ...") answers
-- whether a report meets the requirement: JUST FALSE where a required item is missing (fork F2, a bare "must" not done).
-- Keel answers and answers of other parts are INPUTS named as PLAN.md 4.1 and 4.2 name them.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 495  Auditor's report on company's annual accounts
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 495(1)
-- Plain gloss: the auditor must report to the members on every set of annual accounts whose copies are, while he holds office, to be
-- sent to members (a private company: s 423) or laid before the general meeting (a public company: s 437).
-- src:6973 | (1) A company's auditor must make a report to the company's members on all annual accounts of the company of which copies are, during his tenure of office—
-- src:6974 | (a) in the case of a private company, to be sent out to members under section 423;
-- src:6975 | (b) in the case of a public company, to be laid before the company in general meeting under section 437.
@ref s 495(1) The auditor's duty to report (src:6973-6975)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies are, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be sent out to members under section 423` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies are, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be laid before the company in general meeting under section 437` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(1) the auditor must make a report to the members on the annual accounts` MEANS
    IF       (`s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND `copies are, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be sent out to members under section 423`)
          OR (`s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `copies are, during the auditor's tenure of office, to be laid before the company in general meeting under section 437`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all annual accounts of the company of which copies are, during his tenure of office— (a) in the case of a private company, to be sent out to members under section 423; (b) in the case of a public company, to be laid before the company in general meeting under section 437"

-- The same duty as a deontic rule. No period is stated, so there is no WITHIN (phrasebook 5.9).
@ref s 495(1) The auditor's duty to report (src:6973-6975)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 495(1) the auditor's duty to report to the members` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Member, "make a report to the company's members on the annual accounts"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- COVERS: s 495(2)
-- Plain gloss: the report must say whose accounts, which accounts and for what period, the reporting framework, and the scope of the audit and the standards used.
-- src:6976 | (2) The auditor’s report must include—
-- src:6977 | (a) the identity of the company whose annual accounts are the subject of the audit,
-- src:6978 | (b) a description of the annual accounts that are the subject of the audit (including the period covered by those accounts),
-- src:6979 | (c) a description of the financial reporting framework that has been applied in the preparation of those accounts, and
-- src:6980 | (d) a description of the scope of the audit identifying the auditing standards in accordance with which the audit was conducted.
@ref s 495(2) What the auditor's report must include (src:6976-6980)
GIVEN `the report includes the identity of the company whose annual accounts are the subject of the audit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a description of the annual accounts that are the subject of the audit (including the period covered by those accounts)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a description of the financial reporting framework that has been applied in the preparation of those accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a description of the scope of the audit identifying the auditing standards in accordance with which the audit was conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(2) the auditor's report includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the report includes the identity of the company whose annual accounts are the subject of the audit`
         AND `the report includes a description of the annual accounts that are the subject of the audit (including the period covered by those accounts)`
         AND `the report includes a description of the financial reporting framework that has been applied in the preparation of those accounts`
         AND `the report includes a description of the scope of the audit identifying the auditing standards in accordance with which the audit was conducted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The auditor’s report must include— (a) the identity of the company ... (b) a description of the annual accounts ... (c) a description of the financial reporting framework ... (d) a description of the scope of the audit" (fork F2: a bare "must" not done)

-- COVERS: s 495(3)
-- Plain gloss: the report must say clearly, as the auditor's opinion, whether the accounts give a true and fair view (of the balance sheet, the profit and loss account, or the group), whether they were properly prepared under the framework, and whether they meet this Act.
-- src:6981 | (3) The report must state clearly whether, in the auditor's opinion, the annual accounts—
-- src:6982 | (a) give a true and fair view—
-- src:6983 | (i) in the case of an individual balance sheet, of the state of affairs of the company as at the end of the financial year,
-- src:6984 | (ii) in the case of an individual profit and loss account, of the profit or loss of the company for the financial year,
-- src:6985 | (iii) in the case of group accounts, of the state of affairs as at the end of the financial year and of the profit or loss for the financial year of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company;
-- src:6986 | (b) have been properly prepared in accordance with the relevant financial reporting framework; and
-- src:6987 | (c) have been prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Act ....
@ref s 495(3) Opinions the report must state (src:6981-6987)
GIVEN `the annual accounts include an individual balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the annual accounts include an individual profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the annual accounts are group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the individual balance sheet gives a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the company as at the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the individual profit and loss account gives a true and fair view of the profit or loss of the company for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the group accounts give a true and fair view of the state of affairs as at the end of the financial year and of the profit or loss for the financial year of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the annual accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with the relevant financial reporting framework` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the annual accounts have been prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(3) the report states clearly each opinion the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       ((NOT `the annual accounts include an individual balance sheet`)
              OR `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the individual balance sheet gives a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the company as at the end of the financial year`)
         AND ((NOT `the annual accounts include an individual profit and loss account`)
              OR `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the individual profit and loss account gives a true and fair view of the profit or loss of the company for the financial year`)
         AND ((NOT `the annual accounts are group accounts`)
              OR `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the group accounts give a true and fair view of the state of affairs as at the end of the financial year and of the profit or loss for the financial year of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company`)
         AND `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the annual accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with the relevant financial reporting framework`
         AND `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, the annual accounts have been prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must state clearly whether, in the auditor's opinion, the annual accounts— (a) give a true and fair view— (i) in the case of an individual balance sheet ... (ii) ... (iii) ...; (b) have been properly prepared ...; and (c) have been prepared in accordance with the requirements of this Act" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 495(3)#L6988
-- Plain gloss: an expression in (3) or (3A) that Part 15 defines (ss 464, 471, 474) means what Part 15 says.
-- src:6988 | Expressions used in this subsectionor subsection (3A) that are defined for the purposes of Part 15 (see sections 464, 471 and 474) have the same meaning as in that Part.
@ref s 495(3) closing words: Part 15 meanings (src:6988-6988)
GIVEN `the expression is defined for the purposes of Part 15 (see sections 464, 471 and 474)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(3) the expression has the same meaning as in Part 15` MEANS
    IF `the expression is defined for the purposes of Part 15 (see sections 464, 471 and 474)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks only of expressions "that are defined for the purposes of Part 15"; what any other expression means is not said

-- s 495(3A): a micro-entity's auditors, and what they do with a provision of an accounting standard.
DECLARE `s 495(3A) what the auditors do with the provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 495(3A) the auditors must disregard the provision`
    `s 495(3A) the auditors must have regard to the provision`
    `s 495(3A) not covered`

-- COVERS: s 495(3A)
-- Plain gloss: for a micro-entity, the auditors must disregard accounting-standard provisions that would force extra information beyond the minimum items, and must have regard to provisions about any extra item the accounts do contain.
-- src:6989 | (3A) The following provisions apply to the auditors of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year (see sections 384A and 384B) in their consideration of whether the Companies Act individual accounts of the company for that year give a true and fair view as mentioned in subsection (3)(a)—
-- src:6990 | (a) where the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items, the auditors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain information additional to those items,
-- src:6991 | (b) in relation to a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts, the auditors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain further information in relation to that item, and
-- src:6992 | (c) where the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items, the auditors must have regard to any provision of an accounting standard which relates to that item.
@ref s 495(3A) Micro-entities: how the auditors consider the true and fair view (src:6989-6992)
GIVEN `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of an accounting standard would require the accounts to contain information additional to those items` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of an accounting standard would require the accounts to contain further information in relation to a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items, and the provision of an accounting standard relates to that item` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 495(3A) what the auditors do with the provision`
`s 495(3A) the auditors' treatment of the provision of an accounting standard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items`
               AND `the provision of an accounting standard would require the accounts to contain information additional to those items`
               THEN `s 495(3A) the auditors must disregard the provision`
            IF `the provision of an accounting standard would require the accounts to contain further information in relation to a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts`
               THEN `s 495(3A) the auditors must disregard the provision`
            IF `the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items, and the provision of an accounting standard relates to that item`
               THEN `s 495(3A) the auditors must have regard to the provision`
            OTHERWISE `s 495(3A) not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): each of (a), (b) and (c) is a case ("where ..., in relation to ..., where ...") and the provision falls in none of them
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 495(3A) not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the auditors of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year"; the provisions apply only to such a company's auditors, and the text says nothing about any other
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 495(3A) not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company qualifies is sections 384A and 384B (coa8), not known

-- s 495(4): what else the report must be, say and identify.
-- COVERS: s 495(4)(a)
-- Plain gloss: the report is either unqualified or qualified. Section 539 defines "qualified" as not stating the auditor's unqualified opinion, so every report is one or the other.
-- src:6993 | (4) The auditor’s report—
-- src:6994 | (a) must be either unqualified or qualified,
@ref s 495(4)(a) The report is unqualified or qualified (src:6993-6994)
GIVEN `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared under the corresponding legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(4)(a) the report is either unqualified or qualified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 539 the report or statement is qualified` `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` `the undertaking is not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act` `the report states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared under the corresponding legislation`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- the report is qualified: one of the two the paragraph allows
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the report is unqualified: the other one the paragraph allows
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "unqualified" is not defined; section 539 defines "qualified" only

-- COVERS: s 495(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: if the auditor wishes to draw attention to matters by way of emphasis without qualifying the report, the report must refer to them.
-- src:6995 | (b) must include a reference to any matters to which the auditor wishes to draw attention by way of emphasis without qualifying the report,
@ref s 495(4)(b) Reference to matters drawn attention to by way of emphasis (src:6995-6995)
GIVEN `the auditor wishes to draw attention to a matter by way of emphasis without qualifying the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a reference to that matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(4)(b) the report includes the reference the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the auditor wishes to draw attention to a matter by way of emphasis without qualifying the report`
    THEN IF `the report includes a reference to that matter`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include a reference to any matters to which the auditor wishes to draw attention by way of emphasis without qualifying the report" (fork F2)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- there is no such matter, so the paragraph requires no reference

-- COVERS: s 495(4)(c)
-- Plain gloss: the report must include a statement on any material uncertainty that may cast significant doubt on the company's ability to continue as a going concern.
-- src:6996 | (c) must include a statement on any material uncertainty relating to events or conditions that may cast significant doubt about the company’s ability to continue to adopt the going concern basis of accounting, and
@ref s 495(4)(c) Statement on material uncertainty about going concern (src:6996-6996)
GIVEN `there is a material uncertainty relating to events or conditions that may cast significant doubt about the company's ability to continue to adopt the going concern basis of accounting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a statement on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(4)(c) the report includes the going concern statement the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `there is a material uncertainty relating to events or conditions that may cast significant doubt about the company's ability to continue to adopt the going concern basis of accounting`
    THEN IF `the report includes a statement on it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include a statement on any material uncertainty relating to events or conditions that may cast significant doubt" (fork F2)
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- there is no such uncertainty, so the paragraph requires no statement

-- COVERS: s 495(4)(d)
-- Plain gloss: the report must identify where the auditor is established.
-- src:6997 | (d) must identify the auditor’s place of establishment.
@ref s 495(4)(d) The auditor's place of establishment (src:6997-6997)
GIVEN `the report identifies the auditor's place of establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(4)(d) the report identifies the auditor's place of establishment` MEANS
    IF `the report identifies the auditor's place of establishment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must identify the auditor’s place of establishment" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 495(4) | s 495(4)(a) the report is either unqualified or qualified; s 495(4)(b) the report includes the reference the paragraph requires; s 495(4)(c) the report includes the going concern statement the paragraph requires; s 495(4)(d) the report identifies the auditor's place of establishment
-- (the lead-in line "The auditor's report—" is covered by the four paragraph functions above)

-- s 495(5): several persons appointed as auditor.
-- COVERS: s 495(5)
-- Plain gloss: where more than one person is appointed auditor they make one joint report; it says whether they all agree, and if they cannot agree it gives each person's opinion and the reasons for the disagreement.
-- src:6998 | (5) Where more than one person is appointed as an auditor—
-- src:6999 | (a) all the persons appointed must jointly make a report under this section and the report must include a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the matters contained in the report, and
-- src:7000 | (b) if all the persons appointed cannot agree on the matters contained in the report, the report must include the opinions of each person appointed and give reasons for the disagreement.
@ref s 495(5) Joint appointment: a joint report (src:6998-7000)
GIVEN `more than one person is appointed as an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(5) the persons appointed must jointly make a report` MEANS
    IF `more than one person is appointed as an auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where more than one person is appointed as an auditor—" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where": when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE)

@ref s 495(5)(a)-(b) Joint report: statements about agreement (src:6999-7000)
GIVEN `all the persons appointed make the report jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the matters contained in the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the persons appointed cannot agree on the matters contained in the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes the opinions of each person appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives reasons for the disagreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 495(5) the joint report includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `all the persons appointed make the report jointly`
         AND `the report includes a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the matters contained in the report`
         AND ((NOT `all the persons appointed cannot agree on the matters contained in the report`)
              OR (`the report includes the opinions of each person appointed` AND `the report gives reasons for the disagreement`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all the persons appointed must jointly make a report under this section and the report must include a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree ... if all the persons appointed cannot agree ..., the report must include the opinions of each person appointed and give reasons for the disagreement" (fork F2)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 496  Auditor's report on strategic report and on directors' report
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 496(1)
-- Plain gloss: the report on the accounts must also say whether the strategic report and directors' report are consistent with the accounts and prepared as the law requires, whether the auditor found material misstatements in them and, if so, what kind.
-- src:7002 | (1) In his report on the company's annual accounts, the auditor must-
-- src:7003 | (a) state whether, in his opinion, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit—
-- src:7004 | (i) the information given in the strategic report (if any) and the directors’ report for the financial year for which the accounts are prepared is consistent with those accounts, and
-- src:7005 | (ii) any such strategic report and the directors’ report have been prepared in accordance with applicable legal requirements,
-- src:7006 | (b) state whether, in the light of the knowledge and understanding of the company and its environment obtained in the course of the audit, he has identified material misstatements in the strategic report (if any) and the directors’ report, and
-- src:7007 | (c) if applicable, give an indication of the nature of each of the misstatements referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 496(1) Report on the strategic report and the directors' report (src:7002-7007)
GIVEN `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, the information given in the strategic report (if any) and the directors' report is consistent with the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, any such strategic report and the directors' report have been prepared in accordance with applicable legal requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether the auditor has identified material misstatements in the strategic report (if any) and the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has identified material misstatements in the strategic report or the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives an indication of the nature of each of those misstatements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 496(1) the report includes the statements the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, the information given in the strategic report (if any) and the directors' report is consistent with the accounts`
         AND `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, any such strategic report and the directors' report have been prepared in accordance with applicable legal requirements`
         AND `the report states whether the auditor has identified material misstatements in the strategic report (if any) and the directors' report`
         AND ((NOT `the auditor has identified material misstatements in the strategic report or the directors' report`)
              OR `the report gives an indication of the nature of each of those misstatements`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the auditor must- (a) state whether, in his opinion ... (b) state whether ... he has identified material misstatements ..., and (c) if applicable, give an indication of the nature of each of the misstatements" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 496(2)
-- Plain gloss: with joint auditors, the report says whether they all agree on those statements and, if not, gives each one's opinion and the reasons.
-- src:7008 | (2) Where more than one person is appointed as auditor, the report must include a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the statements and indications given under subsection (1) and, if they cannot agree on those statements and indications, the report must include the opinions of each person appointed and give reasons for the disagreement.
@ref s 496(2) Joint auditors (src:7008-7008)
GIVEN `more than one person is appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 496(2) the persons appointed must include a statement as to whether they agree` MEANS
    IF `more than one person is appointed as auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where more than one person is appointed as auditor," (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")

@ref s 496(2) Joint auditors: the statement about agreement (src:7008-7008)
GIVEN `the report includes a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the statements and indications given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons appointed cannot agree on those statements and indications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes the opinions of each person appointed and gives reasons for the disagreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 496(2) the joint report includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the report includes a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the statements and indications given under subsection (1)`
         AND ((NOT `the persons appointed cannot agree on those statements and indications`)
              OR `the report includes the opinions of each person appointed and gives reasons for the disagreement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the report must include a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree ... and, if they cannot agree ..., the report must include the opinions of each person appointed and give reasons for the disagreement" (fork F2)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 497  Auditor's report on auditable part of directors' remuneration report
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 497(1)
-- Plain gloss: for a quoted company the auditor must report to the members on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report and say whether it has been properly prepared under this Act.
-- src:7010 | (1) If the company is a quoted company ..., the auditor, in his report on the company's annual accounts for the financial year, must—
-- src:7011 | (a) report to the company's members on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report, and
-- src:7012 | (b) state whether in his opinion that part of the directors' remuneration report has been properly prepared in accordance with this Act.
@ref s 497(1) Report on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report (src:7010-7012)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 497(1) the auditor must report on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company is a quoted company ..., the auditor ... must—"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is section 385 (coa8), not known

@ref s 497(1)(a)-(b) Report on the auditable part (src:7011-7012)
GIVEN `the report is made to the company's members on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, that part has been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 497(1) the report on the auditable part is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the report is made to the company's members on the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report`
         AND `the report states whether, in the auditor's opinion, that part has been properly prepared in accordance with this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the auditor, in his report on the company's annual accounts for the financial year, must— (a) report to the company's members on the auditable part ..., and (b) state whether in his opinion that part ... has been properly prepared in accordance with this Act" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 497(2)
-- Plain gloss: "the auditable part" is the part of the remuneration report that regulations under section 421 identify as such.
-- src:7013 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, “the auditable part” of a directors' remuneration report is the part identified as such by regulations under section 421.
@ref s 497(2) "the auditable part" (src:7013-7013)
GIVEN `the part is identified as the auditable part by regulations under section 421` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 497(2) the part of the directors' remuneration report is the auditable part` MEANS
    IF `the part is identified as the auditable part by regulations under section 421`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the auditable part” of a directors' remuneration report is the part identified as such by regulations under section 421" (a definition by "is", read as closed: fork F3)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 497A  Auditor's report on separate corporate governance statement
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 497A(1)
-- Plain gloss: if the company prepares a separate corporate governance statement, the auditor's report must say whether its information (on internal control, risk management and share capital) is consistent with the accounts and legally prepared, whether he found material misstatements and what kind, and whether the other listed rules have been complied with.
-- src:7016 | (1) Where the company prepares a separate corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year, the auditor must, in his report of the company’s annual accounts for that year—
-- src:7017 | (a) state whether, in his opinion, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, the information given in the statement in compliance with rules 7.2.5 and 7.2.6 in the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority (information about internal control and risk management systems in relation to financial reporting processes and about share capital structures)—
-- src:7018 | (i) is consistent with those accounts, and
-- src:7019 | (ii) has been prepared in accordance with applicable legal requirements,
-- src:7020 | (b) state whether, in the light of the knowledge and understanding of the company and its environment obtained in the course of the audit, he has identified material misstatements in the information in the statement referred to in paragraph (a),
-- src:7021 | (c) if applicable, give an indication of the nature of each of the misstatements referred to in paragraph (b), and
-- src:7022 | (d) state whether, in his opinion, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, rules 7.2.2, 7.2.3 and 7.2.7 in the Disclosure Rules and Transparency Rules sourcebook made by the Financial Conduct Authority (information about the company’s corporate governance code and practices and about its administrative, management and supervisory bodies and their committees) have been complied with, if applicable.
@ref s 497A(1) Report on the separate corporate governance statement (src:7016-7022)
GIVEN `s 538A(3) the corporate governance statement is a separate one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 497A(1) the auditor must report on the separate corporate governance statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 538A(3) the corporate governance statement is a separate one`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the company prepares a separate corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year, the auditor must"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the statement is separate rests on section 538A(3) and the directors' report

@ref s 497A(1)(a)-(d) Report on the separate corporate governance statement (src:7017-7022)
GIVEN `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, the information given in the statement under rules 7.2.5 and 7.2.6 is consistent with those accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether that information has been prepared in accordance with applicable legal requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether the auditor has identified material misstatements in the information in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has identified material misstatements in the information in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives an indication of the nature of each of those misstatements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rules 7.2.2, 7.2.3 and 7.2.7 apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, rules 7.2.2, 7.2.3 and 7.2.7 have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 497A(1) the report includes the statements the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, the information given in the statement under rules 7.2.5 and 7.2.6 is consistent with those accounts`
         AND `the report states whether that information has been prepared in accordance with applicable legal requirements`
         AND `the report states whether the auditor has identified material misstatements in the information in the statement`
         AND ((NOT `the auditor has identified material misstatements in the information in the statement`)
              OR `the report gives an indication of the nature of each of those misstatements`)
         AND ((NOT `rules 7.2.2, 7.2.3 and 7.2.7 apply`)
              OR `the report states whether, based on the work undertaken in the course of the audit, rules 7.2.2, 7.2.3 and 7.2.7 have been complied with`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the auditor must, in his report ..., (a) state whether ... (b) state whether ... (c) if applicable, give an indication ..., and (d) state whether ... rules 7.2.2, 7.2.3 and 7.2.7 ... have been complied with, if applicable" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 497A(2)
-- Plain gloss: joint auditors: as in s 496(2).
-- src:7023 | (2) Where more than one person is appointed as auditor, the report must include a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the statements and indications given under subsection (1) and, if they cannot agree on those statements and indications, the report must include the opinions of each person appointed and give reasons for the disagreement.
@ref s 497A(2) Joint auditors (src:7023-7023)
GIVEN `more than one person is appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 497A(2) the persons appointed must include a statement as to whether they agree` MEANS
    IF `more than one person is appointed as auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where more than one person is appointed as auditor," (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")

@ref s 497A(2) Joint auditors: the statement about agreement (src:7023-7023)
GIVEN `the report includes a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the statements and indications given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons appointed cannot agree on those statements and indications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes the opinions of each person appointed and gives reasons for the disagreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 497A(2) the joint report includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       `the report includes a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree on the statements and indications given under subsection (1)`
         AND ((NOT `the persons appointed cannot agree on those statements and indications`)
              OR `the report includes the opinions of each person appointed and gives reasons for the disagreement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the report must include a statement as to whether all the persons appointed agree ... and, if they cannot agree ..., the report must include the opinions of each person appointed and give reasons for the disagreement" (fork F2)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 498  Duties of auditor
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 498(1)
-- Plain gloss: in preparing his report the auditor must investigate enough to form an opinion on three things: whether proper accounting records were kept and returns received from branches he did not visit; whether the individual accounts agree with the records and returns; and (quoted company) whether the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report agrees with them.
-- src:7026 | (1) A company's auditor, in preparing his report, must carry out such investigations as will enable him to form an opinion as to—
-- src:7027 | (a) whether adequate accounting records have been kept by the company and returns adequate for their audit have been received from branches not visited by him, and
-- src:7028 | (b) whether the company's individual accounts are in agreement with the accounting records and returns, and
-- src:7029 | (c) in the case of a quoted company ..., whether the auditable part of the company's directors' remuneration report is in agreement with the accounting records and returns.
@ref s 498(1) The investigations the auditor must carry out (src:7026-7029)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's investigations enable him to form an opinion as to whether adequate accounting records have been kept by the company and returns adequate for their audit have been received from branches not visited by him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's investigations enable him to form an opinion as to whether the company's individual accounts are in agreement with the accounting records and returns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's investigations enable him to form an opinion as to whether the auditable part of the company's directors' remuneration report is in agreement with the accounting records and returns` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498(1) the auditor has carried out such investigations as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (  `the auditor's investigations enable him to form an opinion as to whether adequate accounting records have been kept by the company and returns adequate for their audit have been received from branches not visited by him`
          AND `the auditor's investigations enable him to form an opinion as to whether the company's individual accounts are in agreement with the accounting records and returns`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must carry out such investigations as will enable him to form an opinion as to— (a) ... (b) ..." (fork F2)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- paragraph (c) is for "the case of a quoted company" and does not arise
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the auditor's investigations enable him to form an opinion as to whether the auditable part of the company's directors' remuneration report is in agreement with the accounting records and returns`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in the case of a quoted company ..., whether the auditable part of the company's directors' remuneration report is in agreement with the accounting records and returns" (fork F2)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (c) applies depends on section 385 (coa8), not known

-- COVERS: s 498(2)(a)
-- Plain gloss: if the auditor is of the opinion that adequate accounting records have not been kept, or returns not received, he must say so in his report.
-- src:7030 | (2) If the auditor is of the opinion—
-- src:7031 | (a) that adequate accounting records have not been kept, or that returns adequate for their audit have not been received from branches not visited by him, or
-- src:7034 | the auditor shall state that fact in his report.
@ref s 498(2)(a) Statement that accounting records or returns are inadequate (src:7030-7034)
GIVEN `the auditor is of the opinion that adequate accounting records have not been kept, or that returns adequate for their audit have not been received from branches not visited by him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498(2)(a) the auditor shall state in his report that adequate accounting records have not been kept` MEANS
    IF `the auditor is of the opinion that adequate accounting records have not been kept, or that returns adequate for their audit have not been received from branches not visited by him`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the auditor is of the opinion— (a) ... the auditor shall state that fact in his report" (fork F1: a duty whose "if" is unmet; marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 498(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: if the auditor thinks the individual accounts do not agree with the accounting records and returns, he must say so.
-- src:7030 | (2) If the auditor is of the opinion—
-- src:7032 | (b) that the company's individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns, or
-- src:7034 | the auditor shall state that fact in his report.
@ref s 498(2)(b) Statement that the accounts do not agree with the records and returns (src:7030-7034)
GIVEN `the auditor is of the opinion that the company's individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498(2)(b) the auditor shall state in his report that the individual accounts are not in agreement with the records and returns` MEANS
    IF `the auditor is of the opinion that the company's individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the auditor is of the opinion— (b) that the company's individual accounts are not in agreement with the accounting records and returns ... the auditor shall state that fact in his report" (fork F1)

-- COVERS: s 498(2)(c)
-- Plain gloss: for a quoted company, if the auditor thinks the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report does not agree with the records and returns, he must say so.
-- src:7030 | (2) If the auditor is of the opinion—
-- src:7033 | (c) in the case of a quoted company ..., that the auditable part of its directors' remuneration report is not in agreement with the accounting records and returns,
-- src:7034 | the auditor shall state that fact in his report.
@ref s 498(2)(c) Statement that the auditable part does not agree with the records and returns (src:7030-7034)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is of the opinion that the auditable part of the company's directors' remuneration report is not in agreement with the accounting records and returns` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498(2)(c) the auditor shall state in his report that the auditable part is not in agreement with the records and returns` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the auditor is of the opinion that the auditable part of the company's directors' remuneration report is not in agreement with the accounting records and returns`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the auditor is of the opinion— (c) in the case of a quoted company ..., that the auditable part ... is not in agreement ... the auditor shall state that fact in his report" (fork F1)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in the case of a quoted company"; the paragraph is for a quoted company
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is quoted is section 385 (coa8), not known

-- COVERS: s 498(3)
-- Plain gloss: if the auditor fails to obtain all the information and explanations he believes necessary for the audit, he must say so in his report.
-- src:7035 | (3) If the auditor fails to obtain all the information and explanations which, to the best of his knowledge and belief, are necessary for the purposes of his audit, he shall state that fact in his report.
