-- COVERS: s 498(4)
-- Plain gloss: if the accounts (or, for a quoted company, the auditable part) do not comply with the regulations on directors' benefits or remuneration, the auditor must give the required particulars in his report so far as he reasonably can.
-- src:7036 | (4) If—
-- src:7037 | (a) the requirements of regulations under section 412 (disclosure of directors' benefits: remuneration, pensions and compensation for loss of office) are not complied with in the annual accounts, or
-- src:7038 | (b) in the case of a quoted company, the requirements of regulations under section 421 as to information forming the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report are not complied with in that report,
-- src:7039 | the auditor must include in his report, so far as he is reasonably able to do so, a statement giving the required particulars.
@ref s 498(4) Required particulars where the regulations are not complied with (src:7036-7039)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of regulations under section 412 are not complied with in the annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of regulations under section 421 as to information forming the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report are not complied with in that report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498(4) the auditor must include in his report a statement giving the required particulars, so far as he is reasonably able to do so` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirements of regulations under section 412 are not complied with in the annual accounts` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the requirements of regulations under section 421 as to information forming the auditable part of the directors' remuneration report are not complied with in that report`
           THEN CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
                WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a quoted company"; the paragraph is for a quoted company
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is quoted is section 385 (coa8), not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If— (a) the requirements of regulations under section 412 ... are not complied with ..., or (b) in the case of a quoted company, the requirements of regulations under section 421 ... are not complied with ..., the auditor must include in his report" (fork F1)

-- COVERS: s 498(5)
-- Plain gloss: if the directors used the small companies regime or the small companies exemption and, in the auditor's opinion, were not entitled to, the auditor must say so in his report.
-- src:7040 | (5) If the directors of the company—
-- src:7041 | (a) have prepared accounts in accordance with the small companies regime, or
-- src:7042 | (b) have taken advantage of small companies exemption from the requirement to prepare a strategic report or in preparing the directors' report,
-- src:7043 | and in the auditor's opinion they were not entitled to do so, the auditor shall state that fact in his report.
@ref s 498(5) Statement that the directors were not entitled to the small companies regime or exemption (src:7040-7043)
GIVEN `the directors have prepared accounts in accordance with the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have taken advantage of small companies exemption from the requirement to prepare a strategic report or in preparing the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the auditor's opinion the directors were not entitled to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498(5) the auditor shall state in his report that the directors were not entitled to do so` MEANS
    IF       (`the directors have prepared accounts in accordance with the small companies regime`
              OR `the directors have taken advantage of small companies exemption from the requirement to prepare a strategic report or in preparing the directors' report`)
         AND `in the auditor's opinion the directors were not entitled to do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the directors of the company— (a) have prepared accounts in accordance with the small companies regime, or (b) have taken advantage of small companies exemption ..., and in the auditor's opinion they were not entitled to do so, the auditor shall state that fact in his report" (fork F1)

