-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 498A  Auditor's duties in relation to separate corporate governance statement
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 498A#L7047, s 498A(a)
-- Plain gloss: where the company must prepare a corporate governance statement and none is in the directors' report, the auditor must find out whether one has been prepared.
-- src:7047 | Where the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year and no such statement is included in the directors' report—
-- src:7048 | (a) the company's auditor, in preparing his report on the company's annual accounts for that year, must ascertain whether a corporate governance statement has been prepared, and
@ref s 498A(a) Duty to ascertain whether a corporate governance statement has been prepared (src:7047-7048)
GIVEN `the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no such statement is included in the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498A(a) the auditor must ascertain whether a corporate governance statement has been prepared` MEANS
    IF `the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year` AND `no such statement is included in the directors' report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year and no such statement is included in the directors' report—" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")

-- COVERS: s 498A(b)
-- Plain gloss: and if it appears to him that none has been prepared, he must say so in his report.
-- src:7047 | Where the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year and no such statement is included in the directors' report—
-- src:7049 | (b) if it appears to the auditor that no such statement has been prepared, he must state that fact in his report.
@ref s 498A(b) Statement that no corporate governance statement has been prepared (src:7047-7049)
GIVEN `the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no such statement is included in the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the auditor that no such statement has been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 498A(b) the auditor must state in his report that no corporate governance statement has been prepared` MEANS
    IF       `the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement in respect of a financial year`
         AND `no such statement is included in the directors' report`
         AND `it appears to the auditor that no such statement has been prepared`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the company is required to prepare a corporate governance statement ... and no such statement is included in the directors' report— ... (b) if it appears to the auditor that no such statement has been prepared, he must state that fact in his report" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where"; fork F1)
